      "content": "It's not advisable to self-adjust your medication doses, especially when managing chronic conditions with medications like adderall and thyroid meds. Changes in your medication dosage can lead to unpredictable effects and potentially dangerous health consequences. The safest approach is to discuss your symptoms with your doctor as soon as possible, even if it's just ahead of your scheduled appointment or even in between. They can provide an immediate and safe plan to address your concerns. Never alter your medication dosage on your own.",
